[size=4][b]A floor overhead keeps the rain off, and a fire sits on the floor you built for it.[/b][/size]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jekkle/cartur-flooring/master/media/nexus-header.png[/img]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jekkle/cartur-flooring/master/media/nexus-gallery.png[/img]

[size=4][b]Floors count as roof[/b][/size]

Build a second storey and the room underneath still soaks. Your fire goes out, your walls take rain damage, and you stand indoors with the wet debuff on.

Valheim decides "am I under cover" by casting straight up and taking the first collider that is [b]not tagged leaky[/b]. The wood, ashwood and iron floor pieces ship with that tag; stone and grausten floors do not, which is why those have always sheltered you and the wooden ones never have.

This clears the tag on floor pieces. Rain damage, fire wetness and the shelter status all read that one check, so all three follow at once.

[size=4][b]Fires on floors[/b][/size]

Campfires, hearths, bonfires and braziers refuse to leave bare earth. Three prefab flags do that - notOnWood, groundOnly and groundPiece - and all three are cleared on anything the game counts as a fire.

Smelters, charcoal kilns, blast furnaces, windmills and spinning wheels get the same treatment, plus one more thing they need: a stone station standing on a wooden floor would otherwise be demolished by the game's own support check within a tick. That check is switched off for those pieces. Support is still calculated; it just no longer knocks your smelter down.

Everything else about placement is untouched - it still needs support, it still cannot overlap, and smoke still has to get out.

[size=4][b]Floors stop rotting[/b][/size]

A floor is the one piece that usually has open sky above it - a deck, a jetty, a bridge - so it fails the roof check forever and takes rain damage forever. Floor pieces are now exempt from that rain damage.

They still darken when it rains, they still fall down without support, and they still refuse to catch fire while wet. Only the rot is gone.

[size=4][b]Config[/b][/size]

BepInEx/config/com.jekkle.valheim.carturflooring.cfg, written on first run.

[list]
[*][b]FloorsAreRoofs[/b] (default true) - floor tiles shelter the room below.[/*]
[*][b]FiresOnFloors[/b] (default true) - fireplace pieces place on floors, not just bare ground.[/*]
[*][b]SmeltersOnFloors[/b] (default true) - smelters, kilns and blast furnaces place on floors.[/*]
[*][b]FloorsDontDecay[/b] (default true) - floor tiles take no rain damage.[/*]
[/list]

The first three are made once to the shared prefabs at world load, so [b]those toggles take effect after a game restart[/b] - turning one off mid-session cannot put the prefab back. FloorsDontDecay is read as the game runs and takes effect immediately.

[size=4][b]Worth knowing[/b][/size]

[b]Existing buildings get it too.[/b] The change is made to the prefabs before anything is spawned from them, so floors already standing in your world behave the same as ones you place afterwards. No rebuilding.

[b]Smoke still matters.[/b] A fire indoors with no smoke outlet will still choke you. Nothing here touches the smoke system.

[b]Multiplayer: install it on every client.[/b] Each client edits its own copy of the prefabs, so a player without the mod still sees rain come through their floors. Nothing is synced and nothing conflicts.

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]

No transpilers and no method is replaced. A postfix on ZNetScene.Awake edits prefab data once and then does nothing for the rest of the session. The one ongoing patch is a prefix on WearNTear.UpdateWear that, for floor pieces, holds the rain timer the game itself already keeps - a single field write, no reflection and no allocation, on a method Valheim spreads across frames anyway. Mods that add their own floor pieces are covered automatically if they set the game's Floor usage flag, and modded fireplaces are covered if they use the Fireplace component.

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]

Requires BepInEx. Unpack into your Valheim folder so the DLL lands in BepInEx/plugins.

